        "original_id": "faad1276-3b18-54a6-bdda-def7b92b1d77",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: August Wilson, Robert Gossett, Russell Taylor\n- Works: Fences, The Pittsburgh Cycle, A Raisin in the Sun, The Last Minstrel Show, The Closer\n- Roles: American playwright, actor, fictional character, Assistant Chief\n\nFacts:\n- August Wilson was an American playwright born on April 27, 1945, and he died on October 2, 2005.\n- August Wilson wrote a series of ten plays called The Pittsburgh Cycle and received two Pulitzer Prizes for Drama for his work.\n- Fences is a 1985 play by American playwright August Wilson.\n- Robert Gossett acted in the Broadway production of Lloyd Richards's Fences, Hal Scott's A Raisin in the Sun, and Donald McKayle's The Last Minstrel Show.\n- Russell Taylor is a fictional Assistant Chief character in TNT's The Closer, and Robert Gossett portrayed him.",
